Package: kofn
Title: Component Lifetime Estimation from k-out-of-n System Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Alexander", "Towell",
    email = "lex@metafunctor.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6443-9897"))
Description: Maximum likelihood estimation of component lifetime parameters
    from system-level observations of k-out-of-n coherent systems. Supports
    exponential and Weibull component distributions under multiple observation
    schemes: Scheme 0 (system lifetime only), Scheme 1 (periodic inspection),
    and Scheme 2 (complete monitoring). Provides an EM algorithm for Weibull
    parallel systems, Fisher information comparison across schemes, and
    coherent system infrastructure via minimal path/cut sets. The k-out-of-n
    framework unifies series (k=n, via maskedcauses) and parallel (k=1)
    systems as a censoring problem on component lifetimes.
